{
  "_comment": "Configuration for the gate bundle. Every path has a default, and a default that is not there reports NA; a path you write here and do not have is a finding, because a configured path that does not exist is a broken configuration, not nothing to check; and a path that is there but holds no file of the kind the checker reads reports NA too, naming what it looked for, because a rule the tool cannot check must not look like a rule it checked. Defaults: services_path app/services, src_path app, purge_paths [app/purge.py], templates_path app/templates, entrypoints [run.py, wsgi.py, app.py, main.py], dockerfiles [Dockerfile], adr_path docs/adr, gates_path gates.yaml, tests_path tests. Name a path only to move it. waivers is the one way to say not yet: a list of objects, each with gate (a scan this bundle runs), reason, until (YYYY-MM-DD, in force through that day, UTC), decided_by and, optionally, scope (one file or directory; without it the whole gate). A waived finding is printed as waived and does not fail the run, every run that declares a waiver prints what it excused, an expired waiver is a finding and excuses nothing, and a waiver with a field missing is a finding too, never a silent excuse. Every value has a shape, and the shape is part of the configuration: services_path, src_path, templates_path, adr_path, gates_path and tests_path take one path; purge_paths, entrypoints, dockerfiles and preflight_jobs take a list of names. A value of the wrong shape is a finding that names the key, never a traceback and never a silent pass \u2014 a single glob written where the list of purge_paths exemptions goes was read one character at a time, and the `*` among those characters exempted every file in the tree. So is a path that leads outside the project: a checker only judges files the project owns. purge_paths is the one value not joined to the root \u2014 its patterns are matched against paths already found inside src_path. And a file here that cannot be read as a configuration at all \u2014 malformed, empty, or parsing to anything but an object \u2014 is exit 2, because a scanner that could not read its configuration has judged nothing.",
  "preflight_jobs": [
    "scans"
  ]
}
